    "created_at": "2020-02-13T19:34:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-02-13T19:34:41Z",
    "body": "If a Worker and the main thread are both calling requestAnimationFrame, it sounds like there's no mechanism to ensure that they fire at approximately the same time, i.e. the 'now' timestamps will not be the same.\r\n\r\nSeems that would make it hard for a worker to do something like update game state for a known target time. It would also be hard to ensure that a worker gets its perf-frame computation done at some point before the main thread's rAF. That makes me wonder what the point of rAF in the worker is; seems like any implementation that cares about synchronization with rendering should just message back and forth.",
