    "body": "> My mental model, which might be completely wrong, is that assuming the rendering is at a fixed interval, and you have a window event-loop and a dedicated worker loop(or perhaps even others, what about cross-site iframes?) all running rafs, then you can have each loop run rafs at it's own rate, and then at each \"rendering interval\", you batch all the rendering side-effects of all rafs in all loops that have run until then(without needing to have loops synchronize their rafs).\r\n\r\nYes, this is correct, assuming both composition and animation frames are aligned to the same (likely v-sync driven) timer.",
